@ Index:    [Game] The Hunt for the Jabberwocky
@ Author:   pyjam
@ Source:   https://forum.swissmicros.com/viewtopic.php?f=48&t=3749
@ Version:  1
@ Modified: -
@ Tested:   jaymos

@ The Hunt for the Jabberwocky is a very simple game for R47/C47.
@ The Jabberwocky appears at an unknown altitude between 1000 and 3000 meters (this Swiss device only works in meters).
@ The hunt begins at 2000 m, and the C47 automatically indicates the creature's direction.
@ Enter a new search altitude and press 𝚁/𝚂 resolutely.
@ The C47 indicates the new direction to follow.
@ There are 4 distance indicators:
@ ? - out of range
@ 🠙🠙🠙 / 🠛🠛🠛 - from 100 to 999 m (range limit)
@ 🠙🠙 / 🠛🠛 - from 10 to 99 m
@ 🠙 / 🠛 - from 1 to 9 m
@ Warning: if the distance was less than 100 m, the Jabberwocky saw you and fled. The last measurement is therefore no longer accurate. To save battery power, you decide to move before taking another measurement.
@ Some old information found in the archives: the creature always flees in the opposite direction, and the escape distance cannot exceed the original distance. So, the closer you are to the creature, the less it moves away.
@
LBL ‘JABB’
  # Hunt for the Jabberwocky
  ‘ ? ’
  STO R01
  STO R09
  ‘ ↑ ’
  STO R04
  ‘ ↑↑ ’
  STO R03
  ‘ ↑↑↑ ’
  STO R02
  ‘ ↓↓↓ ’
  STO R08
  ‘ ↓↓ ’
  STO R07
  ‘ ↓ ’
  STO R06
  CLSTK
  STO I
  ‘Hunting is open’
  2000
  ENTER
  RAN#
  0.5
  +
  ×
  IP
  STO R00
  DROP𝑥
  GTO 01

LBL 00
  RCL R05
  RCL →J
  +
  STOP

  LBL 01
    LongInt
    STO R05
    INCR I
    RCL R00
    𝑥=? Y
      GTO 03
    -
    EXPT
    STO J
    INCR J
    LAST𝑥
    SIGN
    STO× J
    DROP𝑥
    𝑥≤? 1.
      XEQ 02
    DROP𝑥
    5
    STO+ J
    DROP𝑥
    GTO 00

  LBL 02
    LAST𝑥
    RAN#
    ×
    IP
    STO- R00
    DROP𝑥
    RTN

  LBL 03
    DROP𝑥
    ‘ ⊙ ’
    +
    ‘Capture in ’
    RCL I
    LongInt
    ‘ moves’
    +
    +
  END
